e color of an element.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOtherDirection":{"title":"MXLOtherDirection","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLOtherDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The other-direction type is used to define any direction symbols not yet in the MusicXML format. The smufl","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute can be used to specify a particular direction symbol, allowing application interoperability without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requiring every SMuFL glyph to have a MusicXML element equivalent. Using the other-direction type without the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smufl attribute allows for extended representation, though without application interoperability.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOtherDirection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlotherdirection","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLOtherDirection","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"abstract":[{"text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentati